Provenance / attribution
------------------------
WeirdIKE's IKEv2 code (message parsing/encoding, proposal negotiation, key derivation, state
machine, NAT detection) is an INDEPENDENT implementation written to RFC 7296. It is NOT a verbatim
derivative of any CycloneIPSEC file (see PROVENANCE.md for the precise classification). CycloneIPSEC
was studied as a reference to understand the protocol, and the project keeps the GPL license partly
to leave the door open to importing Cyclone code later. Reference / inspiration:

    CycloneIPSEC -- IPsec/IKEv2 Library
    Copyright (C) 2010-2026 Oryx Embedded SARL (www.oryx-embedded.com)
    Licensed under GNU General Public License version 2 (or later).
    https://github.com/Oryx-Embedded/CycloneIPSEC
    Pinned upstream: v2.6.4, commit e549c03f5c72bed8c278578f7129bccd157b1f08 (see PROVENANCE.md).

WeirdIKE is distributed under GPL-2.0-or-later (chosen license). Should any CycloneIPSEC code be
imported verbatim in the future, those files will retain their original Oryx Embedded copyright
notices and be listed in PROVENANCE.md; none are so imported today.

What WeirdIKE changes vs. upstream CycloneIPSEC
-----------------------------------------------
  * Replaces the Oryx platform layer (CycloneTCP sockets/NetInterface, CycloneCRYPTO, Oryx
    os_port) with three tiny injectable adapters: crypto (default backend: mbedTLS), UDP
    transport (BSD sockets / lwIP), and platform (clock). No second TCP/IP stack.
  * Makes the IKE core OS-agnostic and poll-driven (no OsTask/OsEvent), so the same core runs
    on ESP32/Arduino, NuttX and a plain host.
  * Adds an ESP (IPsec) engine with Tunnel Mode (CycloneIPSEC upstream is Transport-Mode only).

Third-party components used via adapters (NOT included in this repository)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * mbedTLS (Apache-2.0) -- referenced by the crypto adapter, linked at integration time.
    Apache-2.0 is compatible with GPLv3; combined distributions are covered by GPL-2.0-or-later
    resolved to version 3. mbedTLS source is not part of this repository.
  * lwIP (BSD-3-Clause) -- referenced by the ESP32 transport adapter at integration time.
